---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactModal from '../components/ContactModal.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Jevans Consulting"
  description="Learn how Jevans Consulting collects, uses and protects personal information submitted through this website."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Header />
    <main id="top" class="privacy-page">
      <article class="privacy-policy">
        <a class="projects-back" href="/#top">&larr; Back to home</a>
        <br/>
        <span class="projects-eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: 26 November 2026</p>

        <p>This policy explains how Jevans Consulting handles personal information when you visit this website or send an enquiry. Jevans Consulting is run by Jason Evans, an independent consultant based near Cannock Chase, Staffordshire. Jason Evans is responsible for the personal information described here. For privacy questions or requests, please use the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>.</p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>If you submit the website contact form, we collect the information you provide: your name, email address, business name if supplied, the service you are interested in, any selected package or plan, and the details of your project. The form also includes a hidden anti-spam field.</p>
        <p>Like most websites, our hosting provider may process basic technical information in server logs to deliver, secure and troubleshoot the site. This can include your IP address, browser and device details, and the pages requested.</p>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <p>We use enquiry information to understand what you need, respond to you, and follow up about the work you asked us about. We do not use enquiry details to send unrelated marketing.</p>
        <p>We rely on steps taken at your request before entering a contract when you enquire about services for yourself. Where you contact us on behalf of a business, we rely on our legitimate interest in responding to business enquiries. We also have a legitimate interest in operating and protecting this website.</p>

        <h2>Who processes your information</h2>
        <p>This website is hosted using Netlify. Contact form submissions are sent to Netlify so they can be delivered and managed. Netlify may process information in other countries as part of providing its services. See <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Netlify's Privacy Policy</a> for details of its data practices and safeguards.</p>
        <p>This site loads some fonts from Google Fonts. When your browser requests those fonts, Google may receive technical information such as your IP address and browser details. You can learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may disclose information if required by law or where necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</p>

        <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
        <p>We keep enquiry information for as long as needed to respond and manage the conversation. If it leads to work, relevant records may be kept for the duration of that work and for any period needed to meet legal, accounting or insurance obligations. We then delete it or securely dispose of it. Netlify may retain submission data according to the account's settings and its own retention practices.</p>

        <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>We do not currently use this website for advertising or analytics tracking. Our hosting provider may use essential technical storage or similar technologies to deliver and protect the site. The Google Fonts request described above is made when a page using those fonts loads.</p>

        <h2>Your data protection rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on the circumstances and the lawful basis we use, you may have the right to ask for access to your personal information, correction of inaccurate information, deletion, restriction of use, or to object to use based on legitimate interests. You may also have the right to data portability. To make a request, use the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a> and explain what you need. We may need to verify your identity before responding.</p>
        <p>You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy if our website or data practices change. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last updated.</p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
  <ContactModal />
</Layout>
